# Google Sheets Sync Process

Owner invariants (tabs, projections, outbox, drain): [`sheet-sync.md`](../../docs/knowledge/services/sheet-sync.md), [`google-sheets.md`](../../docs/knowledge/services/google-sheets.md). Canonical commands: [`domain-commands.md`](../../docs/knowledge/services/domain-commands.md). Ordinary [No-Sync Lead](../../../CONTEXT.md) (`noSyncAppliesToNormalTabs` in `src/services/sheetSync/noSyncLead.ts`) suppresses ordinary lead upserts; ordinary Forms delete normal Forms rows, while ordinary Calls clean Calls, Duplicate Calls and Bad Call Leads; effective duplicate/bad exceptions still project. [Unmatched Call Lead](../../../CONTEXT.md) stays a separate empty-plan skip (`created_on_unmatched`). Call disposition is shared through `leads/callLeadReportingDisposition.ts`, and direct facade entry points enforce qualification.

## Env, modes, quotas

- `TEST_MODE=true` reads `TEST_`-prefixed container ids through `src/config/domain/runtime.ts`.
- Container env names (`src/config/domain/sheets.ts`): `MASTER_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `MASTER_BOOKED_SHEET_ID`, `TBM_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `TBM_PRIME_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `TOP10_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `BEST_RELOCATION_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `GETMOVERS_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `MAINSITE_LEADS_SHEET_ID`.
- `WRITE_SOURCE_LEAD_SHEETS` defaults false (`shouldWriteSourceLeadSheets()`; only literal `"true"` enables dual writes).
- `SHEET_SYNC_MODE`: `legacy` (default / unknown fallback), `queued`, `disabled` (`getSheetSyncMode()`).
- Queue publish (`shouldPublishSheetSyncQueue`): not a Vantage test runner; hosted function runtime (`VERCEL=1` plus `VERCEL_REGION`); **and** non-preview `VERCEL_ENV` (`shouldPublishSheetSyncQueue`). Preview/local never publish. `SHEET_SYNC_QUEUE_LOCAL_PUBLISH` does not enable publish. Topic `sheet-sync-events` / `sheet-sync-events-dev` (`SHEET_SYNC_QUEUE_TOPIC` override). Admin retry starts `runSheetSyncDrain("admin")` and does not publish.
- Cron: `router.all("/api/cron/sheet-sync-drain")`, auth `CRON_SECRET` (Bearer or `x-cron-secret`), no-op unless queued, every 5 minutes (`vercel.json`). Consumer: `api/queues/sheet-sync-consumer.ts` (payload ignored).
- Google hard ceilings: 60 reads/min and 60 writes/min per user. Default operational budgets 45/45 (`SHEET_SYNC_READS_PER_MINUTE_BUDGET`, `SHEET_SYNC_WRITES_PER_MINUTE_BUDGET`). Other knobs: `SHEET_SYNC_MAX_JOBS_PER_DRAIN` (500), `SHEET_SYNC_DEBOUNCE_WINDOW_MS` (3000), `SHEET_SYNC_MAX_ATTEMPTS` (8), payload/batch/lease/run-duration envs in `getSheetSyncBudgets` / `getSheetSyncDrainGuardrails`.
- Quota, request-guard and unconfirmed structural delivery deferrals retry in 60s without burning an attempt. Coalesce only `pending`/`retrying`.

## Topology writer fence

- `sheetSync/writerFence.ts` reads the short-lived `SheetSyncLease` scope `lead-reporting:tab-migration`; held leases block lead upserts/deletes/provisioning before Google writes. Queued drains skip before claiming, recheck before delivery, and recheck ownership/fence/deadline at each provider request; outbox work remains durable.
- Deploy compatible writers, acquire/renew both topology and `sheet-sync:drain` leases, wait out older invocations, rename numeric tab IDs and repair derivative formulas, verify, then release. Migration uses operator Google APIs. No public bypass or permanent env flag exists.
- Old Form aliases (`Duplicates`, `Bad Leads`) are never cached; warm writers re-resolve after cutover and provision only canonical titles.

## Queued request/recovery boundary

- `drainer/deliveryRequests.ts` guards every queued provider request, including tab/header helpers and safe explicit retries. Reserve quota per actual attempt; override both Google transport `retry` and `retryConfig`. Do not change legacy/direct retry behavior.
- Append and positional delete get one attempt per plan. Unconfirmed structural delivery stops all further provider requests in that invocation. Defer unresolved targets; retain confirmed outcomes and each logical job's attempt/status evidence. Replan from current Mongo and fresh tab identity on the next durable drain; never reuse old delete positions. Metadata failure after Google success remains recoverable by identity.
- Read exactly one actual `Mongo ID` header; malformed/failed reads cannot prove absence. Validate identity before a cold header rewrite and reuse the read. Shifted legacy lookup remains supported for deletes; refuse a header rewrite that would move identity. Initialize headerless emptiness only for a confirmed newly created tab. Missing/invalid existing headers need operator correction and existing Admin retry.
- `runSheetSyncDrain.ts` plans each claimed logical job so retry hints/tombstones remain independent; the writer coalesces identical physical writes and fans results back. Duplicate claimed keys retain representative-only Daily Operations emission within the drain. Never finalize a subscriber solely because a representative was processed.
- An in-flight request may finish after lease/fence loss; stop subsequent requests and let the next owner reconcile. No exactly-once network claim. Rollback retains durable work/evidence and restores the prior retry risk. Qualification: [handoff](../../docs/efficiency/sheet-sync-recovery-handoff-2026-11-04.md).

## Operational safety

- Before manually changing jobs, count/group by `status`, `run_id`, `operation`, `resource`, `entity_model`, and creation window.
- Prefer `cancelled` plus a clear `last_error` over `failed` when abandoning verified backfill work.
- Never reset stuck `processing` jobs to `pending` until the underlying failure is fixed. The drainer may release leftover claims to `pending` on run timeout by design.
- After cleanup, confirm `processing` is zero and live statuses are expected.

